          %p
            Also, an elementary
            = succeed "-topos" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn ∞
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\infty,1)
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28infinity%2C1%29-pretopos"}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn ∞
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\infty,1)
              \-pretopos
            in the sense of
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Spectral+Algebraic+Geometry"} Lurie 2018
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%C4%8Cech+nerves"} Čech nerves
            or effective
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/groupoid+object+in+an+%28infinity%2C1%29-category"} groupoid objects
            due to similar coherence issues as those of
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/semi-simplicial+objects"} semi-simplicial objects
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+object+in+an+%28infinity%2C1%29-category"} simplicial objects
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/infinitary+record+types"} infinitary record types
          %h2#definition_predicative_case Definition (predicative case)
          %p
            Since there is no consensus even on the definition of
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/predicative+topos"} predicative 1-topos
            = succeed "-topos." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn ∞
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\infty,1)
            %em at least
            the following axioms (which as we have seen above, are all true in the impredicative case although not included in the definition):
          %ul
            %li
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi E
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
              has finite
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-limit"} limits and colimits
            %li
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi E
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
              is
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locally+cartesian+closed+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} locally cartesian closed
            %li
              For any finite family of morphisms
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                      %msub
                        %mi f
                        %mi i
                      %mo :
                      %msub
                        %mi Y
                        %mi i
                      %mo →
                      %msub
                        %mi X
                        %mi i
                      %msub
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                        %mrow
                          %mi i
                          %mo ∈
                          %mi I
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{f_i:Y_i\to X_i\}_{i\in I}
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi f
                        %mi i
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f_i
            %li
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi E
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
              has a
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/natural+numbers+object"} natural numbers object
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/W-types"} W-types
          %p Note that the stronger universe axiom implies, as above, that finite colimits are van Kampen, and in particular therefore that finite coproducts are disjoint. Instead of strengthening this axiom, we could assume explicitly that finite coproducts are disjoint, and then repeat the proof of descent given above.
          %h2#Examples Examples
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                The
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/terminal+object"} terminal
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28infinity%2C1%29-category"}
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mn ∞
                        %mo ,
                        %mn 1
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\infty,1)
                  \-category
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mn 1
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{1}
                is a elementary
                = succeed "-topos." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mn ∞
                        %mo ,
                        %mn 1
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\infty,1)
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/internal+logic"} internal logic
                this occurs when the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/empty+type"} empty type
                is
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/contractible+type"} contractible
            %li
              %p
                %a{:href => "#Rasekh21"} (Rasekh21)
                gives a construction using filter products using which we get a large class of elementary
                = succeed "-toposes" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mn ∞
                        %mo ,
                        %mn 1
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\infty,1)
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mn ∞
                      %mo ,
                      %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\infty,1)
                toposes. To be precise Corollary 2.31 in the paper gives the following construction: Suppose we’ve an elementary
                = succeed "-topos" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mn ∞
                        %mo ,
                        %mn 1
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\infty,1)
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi 𝒞
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/filter"} filter
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ζ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \zeta
                on the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subobject+classifier"} subobject classifier
                of
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi 𝒞
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
                which is product-closed, such that the
                %span.newWikiWord
                  filter quotient
                  %a{:href => "/nlab/new/filter+quotient"} ?
                of the elementary topos of 0-truncated objects
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msub
                        %mi τ
                        %mn 0
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi 𝒞
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %msub
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mi ζ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\tau_{0}(\mathcal{C}))_{\zeta}
                is not a Grothendieck topos, then the filter quotient
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi 𝒞
                        %mi ζ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}_{\zeta}
                is an elementary
                = succeed "-topos" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mn ∞
                        %mo ,
                        %mn 1
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\infty,1)
                = succeed "-topos." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mn ∞
                        %mo ,
                        %mn 1
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\infty,1)
            %li
              %p
                Other ideas for the construction of an
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/elementary+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-topos"} elementary (∞,1)-topos
                which is not a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Grothendieck+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-topos"} Grothendieck (∞,1)-topos
                also exist in the literature. (cf.
                = succeed ")." do
                  %a{:href => "#Anel21"} Anel 21
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Peter+Scholze"} Peter Scholze
                speculates in
                %a{:href => "https://golem.ph.utexas.edu/category/2020/03/pyknoticity_versus_cohesivenes.html#c057721"} this comment on the nCafé
                that the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} (∞,1)-category
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} Cond
                      %mn ∞
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} Grpd
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathrm{Cond}\infty\mathrm{Grpd}
                of
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/condensed+infinity-groupoids"}
                  condensed
                  = succeed "-groupoids" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mn ∞
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
                might form a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/predicative+elementary+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-topos"} predicative elementary (∞,1)-topos
                which is not a
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Grothendieck+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-topos"} Grothendieck (∞,1)-topos
          %h2#related_pages Related pages
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/elementary+topos"} elementary topos
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/predicative+topos"} predicative topos
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Grothendieck+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-topos"}> Grothendieck (∞,1)-topos
                ,
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-pretopos"} (∞,1)-pretopos
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+type+theory"} homotopy type theory
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Awodey%27s+conjecture"} Awodey's conjecture
          %h2#references References
          %p A vague version of the above proposed definition is on the very last slide of
          %ul
            %li#Shulman12
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Mike+Shulman"}> Mike Shulman
              ,
              %em Inductive and higher inductive types
              (2012) (
              %a{:href => "https://home.sandiego.edu/~shulman/hottminicourse2012/04induction.pdf"}> pdf
              )
          %p It was elaborated further in
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Mike+Shulman"}> Mike Shulman
              ,
              %a{:href => "https://golem.ph.utexas.edu/category/2017/04/elementary_1topoi.html"} Elementary (∞,1)-Topoi
              (blog post, 2017)
          %p See also
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Michael+Shulman"}> Michael Shulman
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Towards elementary infinity-toposes
                = succeed "." do
                  %a{:href => "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=ld4YL787dAk"} talk
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Michael+Shulman"}> Michael Shulman
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Peter+Lumsdaine"} Peter Lumsdaine
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Semantics and syntax of higher inductive types
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://home.sandiego.edu/~shulman/papers/stthits.pdf"} slides
            %li#Joyal14
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Andr%C3%A9+Joyal"}> André Joyal
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em What is an elementary higher topos?
                %em
                  %a{:href => "https://www.msri.org/workshops/689"} Reimagining The Foundations Of Algebraic Topology
                April 07, 2014 - April 11, 2014_
                %a{:href => "https://www.msri.org/workshops/689/schedules/18227"} web video
                %a{:href => "https://www.msri.org/workshops/689/schedules/18227/documents/2046/assets/20468"} PDF
                (slides 57-end). This lecture contains a proposed definition that is not an
                = succeed "-category" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mn ∞
                        %mo ,
                        %mn 1
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\infty,1)
                = succeed "-like" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+category"} model category
                = succeed "-topos" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mn ∞
                        %mo ,
                        %mn 1
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\infty,1)
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/natural+numbers+object"} natural numbers object
                be made fibrant). Other than that, the main difference is that Joyal assumes only one fixed universe.
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Georg+Hegel"}> Georg Hegel
                ,
                %a{:href => "Science+of+Logic#LehreVomWesen"} book 2
                of
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Science+of+Logic"} Science of Logic
          %p For an alternative definition proven (in Proposition 4.2) to be equivalent to the one given above, see
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Nima+Rasekh"}> Nima Rasekh
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em A Theory of Elementary Higher Toposes
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1805.03805"} arXiv:1805.03805
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "https://www.ideals.illinois.edu/handle/2142/101508"} ideals:2142/101508
          %p
            The construction of
            = succeed "-truncations" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
          %ul
            %li#Rijke17
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Egbert+Rijke"}> Egbert Rijke
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em The join construction
              %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1701.07538"} arxiv:1701.07538
          %p The construction of natural numbers from propositional resizing and univalence is in
          %ul
            %li#ConstructingNat
              HoTT/Coq library,
              %a{:href => "https://github.com/HoTT/HoTT/blob/master/theories/PropResizing/Nat.v"} https://github.com/HoTT/HoTT/blob/master/theories/PropResizing/Nat.v
          %p The construction of coproducts from local cartesian closure and the subobject classifier is in
          %ul
            %li#FreyRasekh
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jonas+Frey"} Jonas Frey
              and
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Nima+Rasekh"} Nima Rasekh
              = succeed "," do
                %em Constructing Coproducts in locally Cartesian closed ∞-categories
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2108.11304"} arxiv
          %p Results holding for elementary (∞,1)-toposes:
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Nima+Rasekh"}> Nima Rasekh
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Yoneda Lemma for Elementary Higher Toposes
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1809.01736"} arXiv:1809.01736
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Nima+Rasekh"}> Nima Rasekh
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Every Elementary Higher Topos has a Natural Number Object
                %strong 37
                13 (2021) 337-377. (
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1809.01734"}> arXiv:1809.01734
                ,
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://www.tac.mta.ca/tac/volumes/37/13/37-13abs.html"} tac:37-13
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Nima+Rasekh"}> Nima Rasekh
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Truncations and Blakers-Massey in an Elementary Higher Topos
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1812.10527"} arXiv:1812.10527
          %p
            Using
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/comprehension+schemes"} comprehension schemes
            to characterize categorical properties of elementary ∞-toposes:
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Raffael+Stenzel"}> Raffael Stenzel
              ,
              %em (∞,1)-Categorical Comprehension Schemes
              \&amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2010.09663"}> arXiv:2010.09663
              , talk:
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a{:href => "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=qVhRruh_1jI"} YT
          %p
            On
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+type+with+finite+homotopy+groups"} π-finite homotopy types
            as a partial analogue of the elementary 1-topos
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/FinSet"} FinSet
          %ul
            %li#Anel21
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Mathieu+Anel"}> Mathieu Anel
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em The elementary infinity-topos of truncated coherent spaces
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2107.02082"} arxiv:2107.02082
          %p The filter product construction is used to construct elementary (∞,1)-toposes which aren’t Grothendieck (∞,1)-toposes in:
          %ul
            %li#Rasekh21
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Nima+Rasekh"}> Nima Rasekh
              ,
